From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Mon, 12 Jan 2026 23:59:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dpa-app: Fix memory corruption in port info functions

Bug 1 (get_port_info, line 346):
- dist_info offset was calculated using cmodel.port_count (total ports
  across all fmans) instead of 'ports' (ports for this fman only)
- This caused dist_info to point beyond the allocated buffer when there
  are multiple fmans, leading to heap corruption

Bug 2 (update_port_dist_info):
- Loop iterated over all ports (cmodel.port_count) but port_info array
  only contains entries for this fman
- Did not filter by fman like get_port_info does, causing it to:
  - Read past the port_info array bounds
  - Use wrong scheme indices from cmodel.port[ii].schemes[jj]
- Added the same fman filter used in get_port_info to fix the issue

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
---
 dpa_app-4.03.0/dpa.c | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dpa_app-4.03.0/dpa.c b/dpa_app-4.03.0/dpa.c
index 80b5972..c5f0b1d 100644
--- a/dpa_app-4.03.0/dpa.c
+++ b/dpa_app-4.03.0/dpa.c
@@ -343,7 +343,7 @@ static int get_port_info(struct cdx_fman_info *finfo)
 		goto err_ret;
 	}
 	port_info = pinfo;
-	dist_info = (struct cdx_dist_info *)(port_info + cmodel.port_count);
+	dist_info = (struct cdx_dist_info *)(port_info + ports);
 	//scan all ports associated with this fman
 	for (ii = 0; ii < cmodel.port_count; ii++) {
 		sprintf(name, "fm%d", finfo->index);
@@ -410,22 +410,26 @@ static int update_port_dist_info(struct cdx_fman_info *finfo)
 {
 	struct cdx_port_info *port_info;
 	struct cdx_dist_info *dist_info;
+	char name[256];
 	uint32_t ii;
 	uint32_t jj;
 
 	port_info = finfo->portinfo;
 	//update all ports associated with this fman
 	for (ii = 0; ii < cmodel.port_count; ii++) {
+		sprintf(name, "fm%d", finfo->index);
+		if (strstr(cmodel.port[ii].name, name) == 0)
+			continue;
 		dist_info = port_info->dist_info;
 		for (jj = 0; jj < port_info->max_dist; jj++) {
 			uint32_t handle;
-			
+
 			handle = cmodel.port[ii].schemes[jj];
 			dist_info->handle = FM_PCD_Get_Sch_handle(cmodel.scheme_handle[handle]);
 			dist_info++;
 		}
 		port_info++;
-	}	
+	}
 	return 0;
 }
 
